+# #104 ordinary PR tested-merge binding design and replan
+
+[Failed probe](../attachments/github-binding-probe-attempt-1.md) · [Original #104 plan](../plan/implementation-plan.md) · [Parent design](../../103/design/github-ci-quality-gates-design.md) · [Parent plan](../../103/plan/implementation-plan.md)
+
+## Decision and limits
+
+Keep the story branch and its normal same-repository PR into the declared target. Keep the canonical ordinary `pull_request` workflow and its stable `aitm-ci` job. GitHub creates a temporary merge for Actions. The closure owner verifies a GitHub Actions OIDC-backed Sigstore certificate that binds the canonical run and attempt to the temporary merge SHA. There are no extra CI branches, copied merges, branch-management workarounds or direct pushes to protected targets.
+
+In [draft PR #107](https://github.com/kburson/aitm/pull/107), the source commit `d34921e` had one parent. GitHub's [temporary test merge](https://github.com/kburson/aitm/commit/e092c5f387db77d8eb7ac897f801f442097f6b6c) at `refs/pull/107/merge` has trunk `f80f226` as first parent and the source head as second. Neither object landed on trunk during the probe. GitHub's run, suite and job metadata named the source head. The runner's printed merge SHA and the live PR merge field agreed, but neither established an independent attempt-to-merge binding.
+
+This amendment supplies that missing proof for #104–#106. It preserves #103's ordinary PR delivery and the historical design and plans. The manual bootstrap assumes trusted same-repository writers. For changes to workflow or reachable job controls, review the exact source and effective permissions before the authorized push that can trigger Actions. GitHub does not enforce that preflight on other branch writers. For this initial route, hold fork or other PRs lacking the same-repository identity and permission boundary. There are no ruleset or repository setting changes in scope.
+
+## Why this identity is trustworthy
+
+GitHub documents the ordinary open PR's merge ref and `GITHUB_SHA`. Its Actions OIDC issuer supplies certificate identity claims through Fulcio. Fulcio maps the OIDC `sha`, `ref`, repository ID, `workflow_sha`, event and run ID/attempt to signed certificate extensions. The certificate can bind the source and invocation independently of the candidate's logs, JSON and SLSA predicate. The expected PR-specific ref is `refs/pull/<number>/merge` and the exact source digest must equal the live raw test merge. These values are a design hypothesis for this repository's event. A future authorized probe must prove them using the actual certificate and independently retrieved GitHub metadata. [GitHub PR event](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/events-that-trigger-workflows#how-the-merge-branch-affects-your-workflow) · [Fulcio claim mapping](https://github.com/sigstore/fulcio/blob/main/docs/oid-info.md) · [GitHub CLI verification](https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_attestation_verify)
+
+Use a GitHub artifact attestation for the exact bytes of a small sanitized evidence file. The Sigstore bundle supports verification after the OIDC token expires. Verify the signature, trusted Fulcio certificate and authenticated timestamp/transparency evidence with the pinned GitHub CLI verifier and its trusted roots. Plain OIDC bearer tokens are short-lived credentials and stay out of logs and artifacts. A merge object by itself identifies its parents, while an unsigned assertion about that object cannot identify which run attempted it. [GitHub attestation action](https://github.com/actions/attest) · [Sigstore security model](https://github.com/sigstore/fulcio/blob/main/docs/security-model.md)
+
+## Exact verification
+
+1. From the trusted target, authenticate the repository and immutable repo ID, live open PR and its same-repository head, declared target and its live branch ref, canonical workflow ID/path, run, latest attempt, GitHub Actions check suite and required attempt jobs. Select the newest canonical ordinary PR run matching PR number and event base/head, by the original run creation time and run ID. Read its latest attempt after selection. Missing or failed evidence on that attempt cannot be masked by an older run. API run, suite and job head SHAs must match the PR head. Bind job IDs to the GitHub Actions check records and require every applicable job exactly once with success.
+2. Read GitHub's current `refs/pull/<pr>/merge` and authenticated raw commit object. Require its SHA to equal the current PR merge SHA and its exactly two ordered parents to match the authenticated event base/head and live target/head. Record the candidate tree and gate-control blob IDs. An unavailable or inconsistent view holds the gate. A source head, alternate or locally reconstructed merge, or same-tree commit with a different SHA is ineligible.
+3. Retrieve only the selected run's exact attempt artifact and verify GitHub artifact association, name, expiry and archive digest before reading it. Bound the download and unpack only the two allowlisted regular file members, each at most 1 MiB. Reject extra or duplicate entries, traversal, links, unexpected files or malformed ZIPs. Never extract using candidate-chosen paths. Use pinned `gh attestation verify` with the local bundle, expected repo, signer workflow, issuer `https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com`, exact source digest/ref, hosted runner restriction and SLSA provenance type. Use trust roots from the trusted verifier environment and never from the candidate bundle or archive. Require one verified result. Match certificate claims for numeric source repository ID, Build Config URI/path and digest, Build Signer workflow and digest, `pull_request` trigger and exact Run Invocation URI `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/actions/runs/<id>/attempts/<n>`. For the top-level nonreusable canonical workflow expect both configuration and signer digests to equal the selected merge and verify its workflow blob against the reviewed control. Refuse any missing or mismatched signed value. Compare only authenticated certificate extensions for these identities, never values in the signed predicate. A subject digest verifies the JSON bytes, and the JSON still supplies only reported lane, checkout and product evidence.
+4. Independently compare reported head/base/tested SHA/tree, run/attempt and checkout receipts against trusted observations. Require each candidate lane to pin and verify its checkout SHA before work, and the isolated baseline lane to pin the trusted first parent. The signature binds workflow identity and evidence bytes. The approved workflow controls and authenticated required job results establish what was run. Complete the control-blob review and owner disposition before verification and recheck before merge. A full rerun needs all current-attempt jobs and a new bundle. Partial reruns, replay from another attempt and mismatched artifact bytes are ineligible.
+5. If the live head, base, target or merge moves, the old evidence stays historical. Obtain fresh ordinary PR evidence through the existing authorized PR update route. Before a normal GitHub merge commit, reread the exact evidence and use the expected-head guard with trunk rules in force. Coordinate merges into the same target. GitHub's merge API guards head only. Verify the delivered commit's ordered parents and tree after merge. If the target moved in the final interval, hold delivery and escalate the discrepancy without automatic retry or rollback. [GitHub merge endpoint](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/pulls/pulls#merge-a-pull-request)
+
+## Workflow controls
+
+- CI stays on `pull_request` and trunk `push`, with normal same-repository validation on declared targets, no workflow-wide path filter and existing policy for jobs and concurrency. Pin action SHAs and the verifier version, use hosted disposable runners, and keep checkout credentials disabled. Test, build, lint and base-evidence jobs remain read-only and lack identity-token and attestation permissions. Require the real qualified serial Darwin suite, the locked wheel smoke, trusted baseline and subprocess evidence.
+- Keep the original single aggregate predicate over required jobs in the read-only evidence collector. It produces the existing sanitized `candidate.json` with run, attempt, PR, head/base/tested identities, tree, lane checkout and product evidence. Give the isolated `aitm-ci` signing job only the permissions required by the pinned file-attestation action. Budget `id-token: write`, `attestations: write` and `contents: read`, with every other permission disabled. No candidate checkout, scripts, cache, evaluated inputs, deployment environment, repository secrets, storage record or registry push in that job. Use a literal subject path and explicitly disable registry and storage publication. Download only the collector's exact attempt-named archive and immutable artifact ID with a pinned downloader that does not auto-extract. Require digest match and bounded size. Read only one allowlisted regular `candidate.json` of at most 1 MiB into a fixed empty temp directory with trusted inline validation. Refuse other archive members and never interpolate candidate values into commands, environment or action arguments. Pass the fixed validated file as bytes to the pinned signer. The canonical job succeeds only after successful complete collection, signing and upload.
+- The final `aitm-ci-evidence-a<attempt>` archive contains the `aitm.ci-candidate/v2` JSON and a single Sigstore bundle for its exact bytes. The signing job's narrow GitHub attestation write is an explicit scope change requiring future authorization and exact control review before execution. Verify all workflows and referenced controls eligible on the diagnostic PR, with only the reviewed diagnostic eligible for that proof. Keep trunk-push evidence separate. For a trunk push the merge-ref signing requirement does not apply, and it cannot satisfy a PR gate. Retain safe digest, verified claim summaries and archive provenance on planning.
+
+## Delivery replan
+
+- [ ] After separate execution authorization and refreshed #104 JIT, review the minimal diagnostic's exact workflow, permissions and data handling. Run it on the normal bootstrap PR with no `aitm-ci` pass. Collect only a fixed non-sensitive probe file and one bundle. Show actual authentic certificate extensions, exact attempt API link and raw ordered merge parents. Check that a mismatched expected SHA and attempt each cause refusal. If GitHub's signed source SHA/ref, config or signer identity, invocation, archive or permitted signing route fails, record the evidence and return to Planning before production helpers or the wheel. No live proof is authorized by this replan.
+- [ ] If the diagnostic passes and the cap still fits, add meaningful tests for coverage and missing/failing test and job dispositions before building the CI policy helpers. Keep the unrounded **90% line floor** separately for active product packages and first-party executable CI helpers, including unimported source, plus separate branch coverage reporting. Require observable behavior, failure, recovery or invariant assertions. Retain the original exact-base observer, subprocess measurement, Ruff, wheel smoke and macOS capability requirements.
+- [ ] Establish one native negative and corrected complete run, verify delivered source and trunk check, and demonstrate the accepted integration proof with current and refreshed PR evidence after its controlled base movement. Keep the accepted integration proof scope separate from everyday delivery. Finish #104 on its own last gate and sign-off and hand off that proof PR to #105. #105's trusted read-only verifier adds the exact attempt and bundle checks to the accepted negative fixture matrix. Include wrong issuer, repo ID, signer or build config identity, event/ref, source SHA, attempt URI, changed signed bytes, unsafe archive shape, expired/missing archive and certificate verification failure with otherwise green inputs. Use valid signed fixtures or test PKI with explicit fixture trust, never a production bypass. #106 uses the same verifier. Each child closes as soon as its own last gate passes.
+- [ ] Cumulative #104 cap stays 4.0 active agent-hours. Debit 0.35 h for attempt 1 conservatively, with actual engagement Unknown. Forecast 3.45 h remaining active work and at most 0.20 h reserve. Allocate 0.55 h to the diagnostic, 0.50 h to the observer, 0.75 h to helpers, inventory and subprocesses, 0.45 h to workflow, wheel and signed archive, 0.45 h to native negative/corrected evidence, 0.45 h to merge and integration evidence and 0.30 h to review and sign-off. Separate hosted queue time. Reforecast immediately after the diagnostic and split or replan before expanding if the cumulative cap, scoped authority or host assumptions cannot hold.
+
+The previous JIT remains historical. This is planning only. PR #107 stays an unmerged draft. Implementation, a live signing probe, Epic #2 and C01 remain outside this task.
